Corresponding source for version 0.1.0
--------------------------------------
ObsidianCore-Sync-source-0.1.0.zip accompanies the built plugin. A local-test
ZIP includes that source archive; a release-candidate directory supplies it
next to main.js, manifest.json, and styles.css. The source archive contains
the first-party source, build/install instructions, scripts and lockfile.
README.md and docs/release-preparation.md explain rebuilding and installing.
Unmodified npm dependencies are identified by exact versions, download URLs,
and integrity values in package-lock.json; npm ci retrieves them. A fresh
build therefore needs access to those dependencies, not an offline-only
toolchain. The Bridge ZIP also contains its own PHP source and LICENSE.

When offering a binary download, provide equivalent, no-extra-charge access
to its matching source archive at the same place and identify that archive
beside the binary. Preserve the notices. Do not replace matching source with
an unrelated branch or a later build. If you modify a network-accessible
version, review section 13 and prominently offer its Corresponding Source
to users interacting with that version over the network.

